course: dictionary
lesson: 551
title: Attic: a room under the roof
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An attic is a room or space just under the roof of a house. Its name tells you where it is, because it sits right at the top. Clues in the sentence help too: «Raccoons nest in attics and chimneys» tells you attics are high, safe spaces where animals can hide.
explain: Read «In cold countries bats hibernate in caves and attics.» Caves are holes in rock, and attics are part of houses, so both are places where animals can sleep safely through winter. Check your meaning by swapping it in: "they hibernate in caves and in the room under the roof" still makes sense.
explain: Attic can also describe a thing, as in an attic bedroom, which is a bedroom in the attic. Attics can have no proper floor and loose wires, so never go up into one on your own.
fact: An attic is a room or space just under the roof of a house.
fact: People often use attics to store boxes, decorations and suitcases.
fact: «Le grenier» is the French word for attic, and it comes from grain, which was once stored up there.
fact: In stories, attics are full of old trunks and secrets, but in real life they can be unsafe, so children should not go up alone.
fact: «Attic» can describe something too, as in an attic bedroom, meaning in or of the attic.
exercise: «Bats hibernate in caves and attics in cold countries.» What is an attic? | A kind of bat | A cold, dark cave underground | A deep hole in a rock | *A room or space just under the roof of a house
exercise: «Raccoons raid bins and nest in attics and chimneys.» Where do raccoons nest? | In the bins | *In attics and chimneys | In the sea | In the ground under parked cars
exercise: «Le grenier» is French for attic. Where did the word come from? | From a word for spider | From a French king's name | From a word for roof | *From grain, which was once stored up there
test: What does attic mean in «an attic bedroom»? | A bedroom in a tent | *In or of the attic | A bedroom with no windows | A bedroom in the basement
test: Why should children not go up into an attic alone? | Because attics are too tidy | Because attics are always too bright | *Because it can have no proper floor and loose wires | Because attics are full of bats only
exam: Read «In cold countries they hibernate in caves and attics.» What does attic mean? | A hole in the ground for storing food | A bat's hanging perch | *A room or space just under the roof of a house | A cave under a hill
